---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import AdSlot from "../components/AdSlot.astro";
import Economy from "../tools/Economy.svelte";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="WoW: Forever Economy: Trade Board, Gold & Flips | Forever Anvil"
  description="The WoW: Forever auction house economy at a glance: material prices with daily changes, where the gold is, Blackwater flips and Alliance vs Horde price gaps."
  page="economy"
>
  <PageHero icon="economy" eyebrow="Gold & auction house" title="The Economy" facts={[{ icon: "clock", text: "Refreshed about every hour" }, { icon: "economy", text: "Where the gold is, by kind of item" }, { icon: "globe", text: "All three auction houses per ruleset" }]}>
    How the auction houses of your ruleset are doing: what's getting dearer, where the gold sits, and where there's gold to be made.
  </PageHero>

  <Economy client:load>
    <div class="panel pr-help">
      <h2>How these numbers work</h2>
      <ul class="gems">
        <li><b>Typical price</b> is the average of the cheapest 10% of units on sale. One bargain or one silly listing barely moves it.</li>
        <li><b>Gold listed</b> is units × typical price. Anything priced above 10,000g each is treated as a joke listing and left out.</li>
        <li><b>Blackwater flips</b> and <b>Alliance vs Horde</b> leave out thinly traded items. Deposits aren't counted, and a listed price isn't a sale.</li>
        <li>Prices refresh about once an hour. Blizzard's terms let us keep data for 30 days, so history covers at most that.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="faint">Data provided by Blizzard Entertainment. Forever Anvil is not affiliated with or endorsed by Blizzard.</p>
    </div>
  </Economy>
  <div class="wrap"><AdSlot name="bottom" /></div>
</BaseLayout>
